 - [ ] **PREVIEW-001**: When a request identifies an unknown clip revision, the system SHALL return 404 without enqueuing a render job.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-002**: When the requested preview is cached, the system SHALL return 200 with the JPEG for the requested revision and renderer version.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
-- [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict non-pending cache entries (A1in oldest first, then Am least-recently-used) before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: When a completed preview's key is not in A1out (the queue of once-seen discarded keys), the system SHALL admit its entry to A1in.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a completed preview's key is in A1out, the system SHALL admit its entry to Am and remove the key from A1out.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a completed preview's key is in A1out but was discarded from A1out before the render completed, the system SHALL admit its entry to A1in.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When admitting a preview to A1in would exceed A1in's entry capacity, the system SHALL drop the oldest A1in entry's cached data and move its key to A1out.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When adding a key to A1out would exceed A1out's key capacity, the system SHALL discard the oldest A1out key.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: When admitting a preview to Am would exceed Am's entry capacity, the system SHALL drop the least-recently-used Am entry's cached data and move its key to A1out.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-012**: When a cached Am entry is accessed, the system SHALL move that entry to Am's most-recently-used position.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-013**: When selecting eviction victims, the system SHALL never evict an entry whose render job is pending (a shared job ticket is outstanding).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-014**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL remove its key and cached data from A1in, A1out, and Am.
